WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.068
[music playing]

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.436
 Neil, Theo, congratulations.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.472
You've made it into the
finale for this competition.

00:00:06.505 --> 00:00:08.608
It's only one thing
you have left to do,

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.643
and that is to go
back home and recreate

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:17.417
an iconic weapon from
history, the Tai Chi sword.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.488
Emerging from China
over 2,500 years ago,

00:00:22.554 --> 00:00:24.524
the Tai Chi sword is
known as the gentleman

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.526
of weapons due to its
refinement and sophistication.

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:29.495
Symbolizing power and
authority, the weapon

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.531
is one of the most common
ancient weapons still

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:35.234
in practice with millions of
students studying it worldwide.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.370
Fast and light, it's
straight, double-edged blade

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:39.539
was used for quick
stabs and lethal cuts.

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.241
While the sword's fairly
blunt lower section was built

00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:44.010
to block and deflect attacks.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.979
Its reputation is also
preserved in popular culture

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.748
through its role as
the coveted Green

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.683
Destiny Sword in
the film "Crouching

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.752
Tiger, Hidden Dragon".

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:56.455
Your blade must be double
edged, have a winged guard,

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:57.523
and pommel.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.358 line:8%
 Last time I was on the
show, I made an naginata.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:03.096
In comparison, the Tai Chi
sword has a lot more blade.

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:06.365
It's going to be a lot of work.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:07.900
 You will have five
days at your home

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.369
forge to accomplish this.

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:12.038
At the end of five days, you'll
return to present your work

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:13.506
to our panel of expert judges.

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.407
And only after they've
brutally tested

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:17.143
them will they
declare one of you

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:19.278
the "Forged of Fire"
Champion of Champions

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.679
and give you that cash.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:24.250
 I'm concerned because the
Tai Chi sword is really light.

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:27.720 line:8%
I probably have
regular knives that are

00:01:27.786 --> 00:01:29.656 line:14%
heavier than that whole sword.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.891
So that's a challenge for me.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.258
 Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:34.861
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.829
 Good luck, man.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.564
 My name is Neil Kamimura.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.800 line:8%
I was asked to come back,
and I would never say no

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:42.401 line:14%
to my "Forged in Fire" family.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.303
What I feel I've
come back for is

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.039
to represent the people
just starting off

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:49.041
and show them that
you can do this.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:51.444
I've got to build
a Tai Chi sword.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.181
This is the first time I've
ever made something this long.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.181
Holy [bleep].

00:01:56.248 --> 00:02:00.319
But I'm never going to quit.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.855
The blade has to
be heated evenly.

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:06.492
Trying to get the sword lighter
has been kind of difficult.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.827
And being that
this is the longest

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:12.799
thing I've ever heat treated,
I'm not really set up for it.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:19.639
You can feel it
want to bend because

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.641
of the weight of the tip.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.743
So I am scared.

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:28.281
If something goes wrong, I
won't have time to fix it.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.986
My blade is straight.

00:02:34.052 --> 00:02:36.555
I don't have to re-quench it.

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:37.990
I'm stoked.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.492
 My name is Theo Nazz.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:40.893
Winning "Forged in
Fire" allowed me

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:43.963 line:8%
to turn my hobby into a
full time career in knife

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.331 line:14%
making and teaching.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.267
The biggest obstacle
is the raw amount

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:51.037
of forging I have to do then
getting the guard to forge well

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.839
to the blade itself and
then being able to forge

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:55.507
the pommel on as well.

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:57.710
If the welds don't
hold, everything

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.478
will be coming apart.

00:02:59.511 --> 00:03:02.382
How important are
guards on swords?

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:03.916
They can be integral.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.519
Ba dum tic.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:08.655
The quench, big moment of truth.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:12.158
If things go wrong right
now, I've got to start again.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.960
So no pressure.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.402
Perfectly straight.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.471
Things went amazingly well.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.340
I'm happy with the blade.

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.775
If I win, the money would
most likely go to starting

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.343
a new life with my wife.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.179
I had to put that in there.

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:34.780
I'd get in trouble if I didn't.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.648
Oh, God.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:36.983
We're still recording.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:39.485
I'm sorry, Daisy.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.922
 Theo, Neil, welcome
back to the forge.

00:03:42.988 --> 00:03:45.024 line:14%
Theo, tell us about your blade.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.459 line:14%
 It went very well.

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:48.360 line:8%
I did an integral
guard and pummel.

00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:50.363 line:8%
I forged welding
on both of them.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.398 line:8%
The blade's handle
is relatively simple

00:03:52.464 --> 00:03:55.334 line:8%
construction so that it can
be beaten the [bleep] out of.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.971
 You sound monotonically
excited about that.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.706 line:8%
Neil, how did it
go for you, man?

00:04:00.772 --> 00:04:03.709 line:8%
 Same recipe as the
last time I was here.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:06.311 line:8%
Go to the junkyard, get
some stuff because I didn't

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:08.180 line:14%
expect to make it this far.

00:04:08.213 --> 00:04:09.448
 All right.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:12.918
Well, gentlemen, up first
is the strength test.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.087
Ben.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:17.723
 Champions, I'm going to be
hitting this bamboo five times.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.460
Remember, it's not what your
sword does to the bamboo

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:23.095
but what the bamboo
does to your sword.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:23.996
Theo, you're up first.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:24.831
How are you feeling?

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.232
 A little nervous.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.367
Let's go for it.

00:04:35.874 --> 00:04:40.947
[music playing]

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:50.022
 Well, Theo, this is
a brute of a sword.

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.323
The edge held up perfectly.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.058
I don't see any problems.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:54.694
Still straight as an arrow.

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:57.863
The handle is a little bit
difficult to really control.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.932
I would have liked a
little bit more meat on it.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.334
But very well done.

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:03.368
 Thank you.

00:05:03.435 --> 00:05:04.904
 Neil, you're up next.

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:08.507
 Boy, that's a tough test.

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.843
That bamboo setup,
it's literally

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.779
just blunt force trauma.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:16.114
I don't think a lot of
blades can survive that kind

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:19.319
of jarring and punishment.

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:27.593
[music playing]

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:34.600
 Well, Neil, this
sword is heavy.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.869
I wouldn't want to be
running around with it.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.272
There's a little bit of
damage that the bamboo

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.873
gave back to your sword.

00:05:40.906 --> 00:05:42.641
But it's still straight.

00:05:42.708 --> 00:05:44.010
Very well done.
Nice job.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:44.977
 Thank you.

00:05:45.043 --> 00:05:46.379
 Next up is the sharpness test.

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:47.880
For that, Dave.

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:48.948
 All right, gentlemen.

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:51.150
I'm going to be chopping
through these tatami mats

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:52.952
using both edges of your sword.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.854
Let's see if your blades
still have an edge.

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:56.556
Neil, you're up first.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:57.756
Are you ready for it?

00:05:57.823 --> 00:05:59.292
 Yeah.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:01.460
Sure.

00:06:01.526 --> 00:06:03.295
I'm very nervous at this point.

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.231
This is the make it
or break it moment.

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:07.467
I have to perform
well on this test.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.079
 All right, Theo.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.446
Definitely a sharp blade.

00:06:21.513 --> 00:06:23.583
You can see the nice
clean slice and then

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:25.284
burying into the second.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.485
I like the design.

00:06:26.551 --> 00:06:28.254
It's definitely a solid piece.

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:29.855
And that's one of the
nice things about it.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:32.324
I don't feel like it's
going to go anywhere.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:33.058
Well done.

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:34.026
 Thank you.

00:06:34.092 --> 00:06:35.628
 All right, Neil.

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:36.194
You ready?

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:36.962
 Yeah.

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:44.937
[laughs]

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:49.075
[music playing]

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:57.983
 So the biggest thing
is all that weight.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.386
About twice what it needs
to be as far as weight goes.

00:07:01.453 --> 00:07:03.189
It's difficult to swing.

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:05.224
And then the edge
of this blade, it's

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:08.393
got a very stout profile
almost like an ax.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:12.531
Just kept it from cutting
all the way through.

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:15.634
 Theo, Neil, we
took five champions,

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.369
we whittled it down to two.

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.005
But there can only
be one "Forged

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:21.874
in Fire" Champion of Champions.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:26.212
That champion is Theo.

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:27.546
Congratulations.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.582
Neil, unfortunately, your
weapon did not make the cut.

00:07:30.649 --> 00:07:32.451
 Neil, you came
up and showed us

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:34.687
that you had the heart
to make it to the finals

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:36.121
against four other champions.

00:07:36.188 --> 00:07:39.492 line:8%
But your sword took some damage
through the strength test.

00:07:39.558 --> 00:07:41.661
But more than that, it's heavy.

00:07:41.694 --> 00:07:45.931
A Tai Chi sword is known to
be strong, sharp, and light.

00:07:45.964 --> 00:07:48.334
For those reasons, we
have to let you go.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.403
 Neil, please
surrender your weapon.

00:07:51.436 --> 00:07:54.273
 I 100% agree with the judges.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.541
Theo earned it.

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:58.610
But I don't look at this
as a failure in any means.

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:00.779
Because I gave it my all.

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:03.248
I can walk away look
everybody in the eye

00:08:03.315 --> 00:08:04.684
and have everyone's respect.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:08.587
And that's worth more
to me than any title

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:12.425
or any amount of money.

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:14.660
 Theo, congratulations.

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:17.697
You are the new "Forged in
Fire" Champion of Champions

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:20.298
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:08:20.332 --> 00:08:21.567
How do you feel right now?

00:08:21.634 --> 00:08:24.036
 Woo, the nerves and the
butterflies and the nerves

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:24.703
are still going.

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:25.871
But thank you, guys.

00:08:25.937 --> 00:08:28.207
 Please present your
weapon to the judges.

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:31.177
 I [bleep] won.

00:08:31.244 --> 00:08:33.346
My ego was pretty
big beforehand,

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:37.183
and I think this is only
going to inflate it.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.453
Not a good thing,
not a bad thing.

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.188
I think.

